ld simply click on that work list  and every sample that was designed to go  to immunology  would flash so we would quite easily  just highlight those samples pick those  samples that were flashing  and they would set them aside for  immunology or  if we wanted to set up a workplace for  say malarial parasites or im slide tests  again by simply clicking on that work  list if we wanted to prioritize  those it would flash on those samples of  labor parasites so again  we could pick those samples out and  prioritize them so again  it's just improving the efficiencies  within the department  sorry definitely and i think  as you compare through our presentation  that is the main conclusion that we  would come to  we're able to manage ever increasing  work clues  with our automation because we have just  upgraded our automation this year we've  got built-in flexibility now for the  next 10 years  and assuming our numbers keep on going  the way they have been we'll be able to  cope with our workload with the staff  that we've got  we can improve our our turnaround times  because we can't predict what's going on  we can see when samples are going as  well described using our dashboards we  can see if a sample is going to reach  return around time  so that's improving our quality and  decreasing error rates  things like cop recognition help us so  much and  that was quite a common error that we  had in biochemistry before  was that a glucose tube would be labeled  wrongly and analyzed on a gold top  sample  we wouldn't always pick that up at  specimen reception so using the  automation cleverly is a letting that  happen  and so therefore we're maximizing our  efficiency and this allows us to utilize  our skilled staff to do the skilled  tasks that they have been trained to do  thank you and ann and paul for your  informative presentation  we will now start the live q a portion  of the webinar  if you have a question you would like to  ask please do so now  just click on the 